\f0\fs24 \cf0 Working with JC jewelry to create hook lei jewelry brand\
\
This project needed to be flexible. JC jewelry wanted to be able to sell their products securely in larger stores, while keeping true to their brand. These products would be have high interest, but lower risk since they would be for casual use and plated. The other half of the issue was that JC jewelry wanted to share this line in boutiques, shows and events that would also produce higher end pieces that were solid, more luxurious but still held to the same branding.\
\
For this I focused first on name, hoku lei, a shining star. Pieces that would shine and shimmer no matter how high on price point the customer chose and no matter what situation they would wear it in. \
\
Trust is the main promise I wanted to convey in this brand, so we focused on very traditional navy blue, white and with small twist turquoise highlights.\
\
I worked with this company to develop box wraps, bags, inserts and brand direction. }